# MAGGuarantee — backup settings. Install on the VPS as
# /opt/magguarantee/backup.conf (NOT inside the git checkout):
#
#   [ -e /opt/magguarantee/backup.conf ] || sudo install -m 0600 -o root -g root \
#     /opt/magguarantee/src/infra/scripts/backup.conf.example /opt/magguarantee/backup.conf
#   sudo nano /opt/magguarantee/backup.conf
#
# Read by magguarantee-backup.service through `EnvironmentFile=-` (the `-`: a
# missing file is fine, the script defaults apply). systemd reads it as root, so
# root:root 0600 works and hides the heartbeat token.
#
# This lists EVERY variable magguarantee-backup reads. The values shown are the
# script's own defaults — the script (infra/scripts/magguarantee-backup) is the
# single source of truth; uncomment a line only to change it.
#
# systemd EnvironmentFile syntax: KEY=value, one per line, no `export`, no
# ${VAR} expansion (so write full paths, not $MAGG_STACK_DIR/...).
#
# Failure alerts are NOT configured here — see alert.conf.example
# (/opt/magguarantee/alert.conf, OnFailure= → magguarantee-alert@.service).

# ── Offsite ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# rclone remote + path, e.g. gdrive:magguarantee-backups-prod or
# r2:magguarantee-backups-prod. Empty → copies stay on this VPS only (same disk
# as the data) and every run logs a WARNING. Set up with `rclone config` as the
# `deploy` user — infra/README.md «Offsite в Google Drive».
MAGG_RCLONE_REMOTE=

# ── Retention ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Days a dump / MinIO archive is kept on the VPS disk (default 7).
#MAGG_KEEP_DAYS=7

# Days copies are kept in the offsite remote (default 30). 0 = never prune
# remotely (only when the storage has its own lifecycle rule — Google Drive
# does not).
#MAGG_REMOTE_KEEP_DAYS=30

# ── Heartbeat ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pinged ONLY after a fully successful run — a push monitor (Uptime Kuma "Push",
# Healthchecks.io, Better Stack heartbeat) alarms when it stops arriving. This
# is what catches "the timer silently stopped firing", which OnFailure= cannot:
# a unit that never starts never fails. Empty → no ping.
#
# Must be reachable FROM THE HOST, not from a container: Uptime Kuma running on
# `proxy-net` without a published port is NOT at http://localhost:<port> — publish
# a loopback port for it (e.g. `127.0.0.1:3002:3001` on the kuma container, then
# http://127.0.0.1:3002/api/push/<token>) or use an external service.
#MAGG_HEARTBEAT_URL=https://<monitor-host>/api/push/<token>

# ── Layout (change only for a non-standard install) ──────────────────────────
#MAGG_STACK_DIR=/opt/magguarantee
#MAGG_BACKUP_DIR=/opt/magguarantee/backups
#MAGG_MINIO_DATA=/opt/magguarantee/data/minio
#MAGG_PG_CONTAINER=magguarantee-postgres
#MAGG_DB_USER=magguarantee
#MAGG_DB_NAME=magguarantee

# A dump smaller than this many bytes fails the run instead of rotating a good
# backup out (default 10240).
#MAGG_MIN_DUMP_BYTES=10240
